{#
  /noodle-room/. Brief: SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md.
  P0, the growth priority. No keyword target: every handmade / house-made /
  fresh-noodle query combined is 20 rows and 2 clicks over fifteen months. This
  page is justified on AEO, press, and conversion, not search volume. Do not
  set a ranking KPI on it.

  The brief calls this "the highest-exposure page on the site" and it is right.
  Two entire sections of the approved concept could not be built:

    THE FOUR-INGREDIENT BLOCK (flour, water, salt, kansui) is dropped. It
    asserted "a specific Japanese-style milled wheat, higher protein, finer
    grind", hydration ratios, and kansui/alkalinity. CLIENT_FACTS.md: "Any
    claim about flour type, hydration, water, alkalinity, or aging time.
    Nobody has told us any of it." It is also close to a competitor's public
    noodle claim, which makes shipping it worse than merely unsourced.
    Replaced with the two noodle types that ARE confirmed.

    THE HOUR-BY-HOUR PROCESS TIMELINE (06:00 mix, 08:00 rest, 10:00 sheet,
    11:30 cut, 12:00 send) is dropped. Every time, every step, the gluten
    claims, and the per-broth noodle widths are unsourced, and the whole block
    asserts a daily production cadence that CLIENT_FACTS.md explicitly lists as
    unconfirmed. Replaced with the confirmed sequence, which has no clock in it.

  The concept's founder quote was also invented. See the quote section.
#}

